<title>HONG KONG: SCMP (Holdings) 1995/96 net up 20 pct.</title>
<headline>SCMP (Holdings) 1995/96 net up 20 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended June 30</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   44.90	 vs 38.67</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    13.0	  vs 13.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  180.99 gain vs nil</p>
<p>    Net			    695.87	vs 580.06</p>
<p>    Turnover		     1,444.11    vs 1,266.13</p>
<p>    Company name		 South China Morning Post</p>
<p>				     (Holdings) Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  October 28-30</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   November 11</p>
<p>NOTE - South China Morning Post (Holdings) publishes the South China Morning Post newspaper and other publications.</p>
<p>The definition of turnover has been expanded following the acquisition of TVE (Holdings) Ltd  0009.HK and its subsidiaries during the year ended June 30, 1995. The comparative amount of turnover for the year ended June 30, 1995 has been restated to include gross rental income.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain on sale of the group's old headquarters in Quarry Bay.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is 30 H.K. cents (including first interim dividend of six cents, second dividend of six cents and third dividend of five cents) vs same.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
